<title>USA: NFL AMERICAN FOOTBALL-RESULTS OF PAST 30 SUPER BOWLS.</title>
<headline>NFL AMERICAN FOOTBALL-RESULTS OF PAST 30 SUPER BOWLS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>When the Green Bay Packers</p>
<p>play the New England Patriots in Super Bowl XXXI at the</p>
<p>Louisiana Superdome Sunday it will mark the record eighth time</p>
<p>that the National Football League's big show will be staged in</p>
<p>New Orleans.</p>
<p>Following are the results of the last 30 Super Bowls</p>
<p>(tabulate under Super Bowl number, year played, result, game</p>
<p>site):</p>
<p> 30. 1996 - Dallas 27, Pittsburgh 17,	 Tempe, Ariz.</p>
<p> 29. 1995 - San Francisco 49, San Diego 26, Miami</p>
<p> 28. 1994 - Dallas 30, Buffalo 13,	    Atlanta</p>
<p> 27. 1993 - Dallas 52, Buffalo 17,	    Pasadena, Calif.</p>
<p> 26. 1992 - Washington 37, Buffalo 24,	Minneapolis</p>
<p> 25. 1991 - New York Giants 20, Buffalo 19, Tampa, Fla.</p>
<p> 24. 1990 - San Francisco 55, Denver 10,    New Orleans</p>
<p> 23. 1989 - San Francisco 20, Cincinnati 16, Miami</p>
<p> 22. 1988 - Washington 42, Denver 10,	  San Diego</p>
<p> 21. 1987 - New York Giants 39, Denver 20,   Pasadena</p>
<p> 20. 1986 - Chicago 46, New England 10,	New Orleans</p>
<p> 19. 1985 - San Francisco 38, Miami 16,	Stanford, Calif.</p>
<p> 18. 1984 - L.A. Raiders 38, Washington 9,   Tampa</p>
<p> 17. 1983 - Washington 27, Miami 17,	   Pasadena</p>
<p> 16. 1982 - San Francisco 26, Cincinnati 21, Pontiac, Mich.</p>
<p> 15. 1981 - Oakland 27, Philadelphia 10,     New Orleans</p>
<p> 14. 1980 - Pittsburgh 31, L.A. Rams 19,     Pasadena</p>
<p> 13. 1979 - Pittsburgh 35, Dallas 31,	  Miami</p>
<p> 12. 1978 - Dallas 27, Denver 10,		New Orleans</p>
<p> 11. 1977 - Oakland 32, Minnesota 14,	  Pasadena</p>
<p> 10. 1976 - Pittsburgh 21, Dallas 17,	  Miami</p>
<p>  9. 1975 - Pittsburgh 16, Minnesota 6,	New Orleans</p>
<p>  8. 1974 - Miami 24, Minnesota 7,	     Houston</p>
<p>  7. 1973 - Miami 14, Washington 7,	    Los Angeles</p>
<p>  6. 1972 - Dallas 24, Miami 3,		  New Orleans</p>
<p>  5. 1971 - Baltimore 16, Dallas 13,	   Miami</p>
<p>  4. 1970 - Kansas City 23, Minnesota 7,     New Orleans</p>
<p>  3. 1969 - New York Jets 16, Baltimore 7,   Miami</p>
<p>  2. 1968 - Green Bay 33, Oakland 14,	  Miami</p>
<p>  1. 1967 - Green Bay 35, Kansas City 10,    Los Angeles</p>
</text>
